# Timers

Use code actions on a timer or its checklist line to Start, Pause, Resume, or Reset.
These timers are idle until you start them. Save after using a control to keep its state.

## Focus session

[focus_length] := 25m
[focus] := countdown(focus_length)

- [ ] One focused work session @timer(focus) @estimate(25m)

Time left: [focus.remaining]. Session status: [focus.state].
[focus_finished] := focus.done

## Stopwatch

[debugging] := stopwatch()

- [ ] Investigate a flaky test @timer(debugging) @estimate(30m)

Time spent: [debugging.elapsed].
[over_estimate] := debugging.elapsed > 30m

## Quick countdown

[tea] := countdown(10s)

Try Start timer on this line: [tea]. It will reach zero and show done.

Completing a task does not automatically stop its timer. Expiry is visual; there is no alarm.
